# What the server does not need to run.
#
# Railway uploads the repository as the build context, and this one carries
# 130 MB of things that are not the game: the trailer and its stills, the
# responsive harness's screenshots of every resolution, and the packaged
# playtest build. None of it is read at runtime or at build time, and all of
# it is paid for on every deploy.
#
# `railway up` uploads from the working directory rather than from git, so the
# first four lines matter there and nowhere else: without them the upload is
# the repository plus a few hundred megabytes of installed packages and build
# output that the image rebuilds from source anyway.
node_modules/
dist/
dist-server/
.git/

steam/
responsive/
recordings/
release/
release-demo/
release-play/
release-playtest/
playthrough/
playthrough-pad/
res-quick/
plans/
tools/trailer/out/
*.db
*.db.tmp
